From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:02:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l41: Resume the protection firmware on its first
 start

The speaker protection firmware of the Galaxy S10 amplifiers (CSPL,
built for the CS35L40) boots with its algorithm paused and reports
that in the mailbox status.  The resume that turns the algorithm on is
only sent when the DSP was already running, so on the first stream
after the firmware is loaded audio passes through the DSP unprotected:
the temperature model stays at its initial value and the calibration
is never applied.

Send the resume on the first start as well.  The firmware ignores
commands for a while after it reports the pause; measured on the
phone, a resume sent 20 ms after the start is lost and one sent 50 ms
after it is accepted, so wait twice that before sending it.

With this change the algorithm runs from the first stream: the status
reads RUNNING, the modelled coil temperature follows the signal level
and no mailbox errors are logged.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
index b2a076706c7..3739c248ddf 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
@@ -25,6 +25,9 @@
 
 #include "cs35l41.h"
 
+/* time firmware booting paused needs before it takes a mailbox command */
+#define CS35L41_DSP_BOOT_DELAY_MS	100
+
 static const char * const cs35l41_supplies[CS35L41_NUM_SUPPLIES] = {
 	"VA",
 	"VP",
@@ -220,8 +223,19 @@ static int cs35l41_dsp_audio_ev(struct snd_soc_dapm_widget *w,
 
 	switch (event) {
 	case SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU:
-		if (!cs35l41->dsp.cs_dsp.running)
-			return wm_adsp_event(w, kcontrol, event);
+		/*
+		 * Firmware can boot with its algorithm paused, so a DSP started
+		 * here needs the resume below as much as one that was running.
+		 * Such firmware ignores commands for a while after it reports
+		 * the pause: a resume 20 ms later is lost, one 50 ms later
+		 * takes, so allow it twice that.
+		 */
+		if (!cs35l41->dsp.cs_dsp.running) {
+			ret = wm_adsp_event(w, kcontrol, event);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+			msleep(CS35L41_DSP_BOOT_DELAY_MS);
+		}
 
 		ret = regmap_read(cs35l41->regmap, CS35L41_DSP_MBOX_2, &fw_status);
 		if (ret < 0) {
